{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '200,215p' paper.tex; cat global_memory_summary.md; tail -n 26 memory.md; ls global_memory/conclusions.md global_memory/memory.md global_memory/memory.jsonl; sed -n '1,160p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '200,215p' paper.tex; cat global_memory_summary.md; tail -n 26 memory.md; ls global_memory/conclusions.md global_memory/memory.md global_memory/memory.jsonl; sed -n '1,160p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\"","aggregated_output":"Development configurations are informative only as descriptive context. They share influence-prefix constraints but differ in how contenders are screened or refitted. A tied development aggregate for the bounded exact-refit and retained-curvature configurations does not show identical masks, equal runtime, or equivalence on the final partition. No final controlled ablation estimates the effect of replacing the shortlist rule while holding the rest of the evaluated procedure fixed. We therefore attribute the final measurements to the evaluated configuration as a whole.\n\n\\section{Discussion and Limitations}\n\\paragraph{What the audit establishes.}\nA deletion witness demonstrates that a particular fitted ranking is dependent on a particular subset of observed outcomes under a stated objective. Independent refitting makes that finite perturbation observable. Normalization by the number of participant pairs helps compare lists of different lengths, but assigns equal weight to all pair inversions, including changes far from the top. A ranking with a small global inversion fraction can still change an important local comparison. The secondary leader metric partly addresses this issue, without supplying a complete account of top-rank uncertainty.\n\n\\paragraph{What the comparison does not isolate.}\nArena and NBA differ in participants, comparison density, outcomes, content dependence, time span, and preprocessing. Their different responses cannot be attributed to crowd voting versus sports competition alone. The historical team-code model is static across eras, and the largest-component filter changes which participants are included. Equal row fractions do not remove these confounds. No matched-support intervention, expert-versus-model-judge study, or graph-property ablation is available. The scientific conclusion is conditional on these retained graphs, budgets, objective, and deletion rules.\n\n\\paragraph{Restrictions of selection and uncertainty.}\nThe contender shortlist is bounded; within-contender orders remain fixed; selection favors leader demotion rather than the reported all-pairs objective. A weak result can arise from any of these restrictions, and the present evidence does not separate them. The group-weight diagnostic respects declared content groups, not all possible crossed dependence. It holds masks fixed and uses a single stored random-mask family. It neither adjusts for development selection nor supplies uncertainty for attack reselection. No ridge-sensitivity experiment, full adaptive uncertainty procedure, or runtime comparison is reported.\n\n\\paragraph{Sensitivity is not a confidence statement.}\nThe deletion comparison and the uncertainty diagnostic have different reference objects. A deletion witness compares a retained fit with the original clean fit. A weighted draw instead compares weighted retained fits with a newly fitted weighted clean ranking. Thus a change in a conditional gain need not mean that the same participant pair crossed the same original boundary. Rank inversion is also discontinuous in fitted scores: a small score displacement near a tie can change the order, whereas a larger displacement away from a tie may not. The measured inversion fraction cannot by itself identify either the score margin or practical importance of the affected comparisons. Reporting the full budget-resolved curves together with their conditioning assumptions is more informative than treating an aggregate gain or a seed interval as a universal stability certificate.\n\n\\paragraph{Reproducibility and responsible interpretation.}\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-17 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Proposed Dependence Aware Rank Reversal Frontiers; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Untested first-cycle hypothesis has no empirical basis for distilled recommendations.\n  - evidence: Task supplies pinned Arena and MT-Bench human/GPT-4 snapshots. Histories have no prior ideas or attempts. Supplied incumbent correct=true and combined_score=0.01299345456023538; named source path unavailable, with cause unknown. No execution or external research performed.\n- 2026-11-17 | step=final | scope=idea\n  - summary: bundle_ready; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Structural bundle review supplies no scientific validation.\n  - evidence: Required JSON bundles share five rubrics: one canonical metric and four implementation rubrics with 4, 7, 6, and 6 executable patterns. Only canonical idea-local memory targeted; no staging memory or alternate idea directory created. No experiment run or score improvement claimed.\n- 2026-11-17T22:05:02.087050+00:00 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: generated idea bundle (auto-healed by idea.sh)\n  - evidence: idea_bundle.json + target_rubrics.json\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-17T22:08:42.597385+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.013240276724865765, correct=True; scientific acceptance passed; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": 0.013240276724865765, \"completion_rate\": 1.0, \"control_pass_rate\": 1.0, \"correct\": true, \"disagreement_baseline_score\": 0.009313282215679475, \"mean_leader_rank_drop\": 0.01898963542799159, \"paired_gain_vs_disagreement\": 0.00392699450918629, \"paired_gain_vs_random\": 0.006710309257398298, \"random_baseline_score\": 0.006529967467467467}\n- 2026-11-17 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Exact Refit Contender Screening bundle ready; gate=updated; trigger=b; reason=Candidate-source and recorded interface evidence establish an anonymous-row certificate-only regime not covered by any existing distilled conclusion.\n  - evidence: Historical correct=true, completion_rate=1, control_pass_rate=1, combined_score=0.013240276724865765 and positive comparator gains; rubric_overall_pass=false has unknown cause. Prior candidate source confirms clean-Hessian screening, fixed clean-influence prefixes, anonymous inputs, and mean-loss ridge. Selected hypothesis: actual retained-data refits of at most six contenders can improve legal prefix choice. Alternatives rejected for this stage: full all-contender exact refits risk CPU cost; arbitrary swaps violate prefixes; grouped or matched-design analysis lacks labels. No task code, evaluator, benchmark, optimizer, installer, or numerical probe executed.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-17T22:16:49.320744+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.01595532053579999, correct=True; scientific acceptance passed; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": 0.01595532053579999, \"completion_rate\": 1.0, \"control_pass_rate\": 1.0, \"correct\": true, \"disagreement_baseline_score\": 0.009313282215679475, \"mean_leader_rank_drop\": 0.02127274045082264, \"paired_gain_vs_disagreement\": 0.006642038320120512, \"paired_gain_vs_random\": 0.009425353068332521, \"random_baseline_score\": 0.006529967467467467}\n- 2026-11-17 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Retained Curvature Shortlist Expansion bundle ready; gate=updated; trigger=a; reason=Recorded cycle-2 aggregate improvement contradicts the existing conclusion that bounded exact-refit selection remains wholly untested, without establishing broader scientific evidence.\n  - evidence: Recorded cycle-2 combined_score=0.01595532053579999, correct=true, rubric_overall_pass=true, completion_rate=1, control_pass_rate=1; prior combined_score=0.013240276724865765. Allowed candidate source confirms a clean-Hessian six-contender shortlist with exact retained-data refits. Selected hypothesis: bounded retained-Hessian one-step screening can find extra useful contenders while preserving all incumbent finalists. Alternatives: blind expansion is less mechanistically targeted; exhaustive exact refits risk CPU cost; row reordering is disallowed; grouping labels are unavailable. No task program, evaluator, optimizer, benchmark, installer, numerical probe, or literature search executed.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-17T22:25:07.039563+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.01595532053579999, correct=True; scientific acceptance passed; search metrics (data): {\"combined_score\": 0.01595532053579999, \"completion_rate\": 1.0, \"control_pass_rate\": 1.0, \"correct\": true, \"disagreement_baseline_score\": 0.009313282215679475, \"mean_leader_rank_drop\": 0.02127274045082264, \"paired_gain_vs_disagreement\": 0.006642038320120512, \"paired_gain_vs_random\": 0.009425353068332521, \"random_baseline_score\": 0.006529967467467467}\n\n### 2026-11-17T22:47:32.048113+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Repair audit retains the grounded cross-setting frozen-prefix story; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=The sole hard error concerns supplementary source-list schema, not the scientific thesis.\n- evidence: strategy_validation_feedback.json identifies the LLM Usage entry empty source_ids. No paper_data source grounds agent-process roles. Final qualification independently remains completed/qualified; no downstream_study or study sources are present. Existing five scientific supplementary entries have grounding IDs; ICLR requires the separate process disclosure regardless of numerical evidence. apply_patch and system patch executables are unavailable in this environment.\n- next_action: Keep the mandatory LLM Usage disclosure in writer instructions and memo, outside the result-grounded subsection list; preserve all scientific decisions, then run strategy-only validation.\n\n### 2026-11-17T22:49:12.043167+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: paper_strategy_repaired; strategy-only checks passed; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Source-list repair preserves all scientific framing and experimental recommendations.\n- evidence: Both strategy files now distinguish five nonempty source-backed supplementary entries from the separately required LLM Usage process disclosure, retained with its original roles and provenance cautions. Checked output schema, all exact source IDs, memo alignment, figure budgets, qualification agreement, layout/export requirements, and absence of forbidden drafting outputs. One preliminary local check mistook a documented wildcard source-family notation for an exact ID; the corrected checker passed without changing scientific content. No final-paper validation, new experiment, reference retrieval or figure generation ran. Cross-setting frozen-prefix framing remains stronger than unsupported dependence-aware and universal-superiority alternatives.\n- next_action: Hand off repaired strategy; later writing must retain conditional uncertainty, qualification limitations, literature and raw-reproduction gaps, and separate LLM disclosure.\n\n### 2026-11-17T22:51:51.730109+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Independent final audit confirms completed qualified evaluation; retain cross-setting budget dependence and conditional uncertainty as thesis. Gate kept: no new experimental recommendation.\n- evidence: final.qualification.status/outcome; final.evidence.episodes; inspected selected six-contender source and independent evaluator. No downstream study or additional task_names present. Located functional apply_patch executable outside PATH.\n- next_action: Preserve readable source evidence, repair irrelevant bibliography using exact safe foundational identities, generate figures from existing episodes, draft and validate without new experiments.\n\n### 2026-11-17T23:07:43.944738+00:00 | step=draft | scope=paper\n- summary: Standalone draft, source snapshots, two vector quantitative plots, guarded concept placeholder and claim map written. Gate kept: methodological framing adds no new experimental recommendation.\n- evidence: 26 grounded claims and 25 provenance references pass claim validation; section/citation validation passes after inlining supplemental table. Scientific-evidence sidecars corrected to canonical ref tokens; no dangling links. Initial PDF has eight body pages but final-page fill needs additional scientific explanation. Figure validator cannot import unstaged orchestrator module; canonical compile encounters a system TeX symlink audit issue.\n- next_action: Check rendered geometry, finish reproducibility and bibliography consultation audit, validate figure schema and scientific evidence, and repair any remaining hard errors without scientific reruns.\n\n### 2026-11-17T23:15:24.265958+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: paper.tex and claims_grounding.json are consistent with grounded inputs; standalone paper written and locally validated. Gate kept: no new experimental recommendation or scientific execution.\n- evidence: Independent final.qualification sources remain completed/qualified. Canonical section/citation and claim/provenance checks pass: 26 claims, 25 references. Canonical compile and rendered Supplementary Information pass after selecting real system TeX config paths. PDF has eight body pages; local geometric last-page fill estimate is 84.1%. Canonical figure JSON schema, strategy density, source paths, JSON pointers, aggregate reconstruction and visible-language checks pass. Scientific-evidence report has zero dangling links. Opposite conditional dataset signs, deterministic seed intervals, noncausal configuration comparisons, source inspection and raw-reconstruction limitations remain explicit.\n- next_action: Parent workflow should synchronously replace the guarded concept placeholder and run its integrated figure/venue audit. The integrated figure launcher requires an unstaged orchestrator module locally. Raw-source reconstruction remains incomplete and disclosed; no scientific rerun is claimed.\n\nglobal_memory/conclusions.md\nglobal_memory/memory.jsonl\nglobal_memory/memory.md\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Append validated local/global memory entries for idea workflows.\n\nTwo modes:\n\n* default (event append) — appends one memory event to ``memory.md`` (local +\n  global) plus one JSONL record to ``memory.jsonl``. Existing behavior.\n* ``--write-conclusions`` — atomically replaces ``conclusions.md`` with a\n  validated single-paragraph distilled summary and appends a record to\n  ``conclusions_history.jsonl``. Validation rejects empty input,\n  multi-paragraph input, or input over 300 words.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nCONCLUSIONS_WORD_LIMIT = 300\nGATE_TRIGGER_VALUES = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\")\n\nLOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS = \"\"\"# Memory Log\n\n## Context\n## Idea Discoveries\n## Program Evaluations\n## Failures / Regressions\n## Next Hypotheses\n\"\"\"\n\nGLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER = \"# Global Memory Log\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef utc_now() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the current UTC timestamp string.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n\ndef _load_event(*, event_json: str | None, event_file: Path | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Load event.\"\"\"\n    if event_json:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_json)\n    elif event_file is not None:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    else:\n        raw = input().strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValueError(\"missing event payload\")\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"event payload must be a JSON object\")\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef _ensure_required_fields(event: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Ensure required fields.\"\"\"\n    normalized = dict(event)\n    if not isinstance(normalized.get(\"timestamp\"), str) or not normalized[\"timestamp\"].strip():\n        normalized[\"timestamp\"] = utc_now()\n\n    required_string_fields = (\"step\", \"scope\", \"summary\", \"evidence\", \"next_action\")\n    for key in required_string_fields:\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():\n            raise ValueError(f\"missing required string field: {key}\")\n        normalized[key] = value.strip()\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if value is None:\n            continue\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            normalized[key] = str(value)\n        normalized[key] = normalized[key].strip() or None\n\n    metrics = normalized.get(\"metrics\")\n    if metrics is not None and not isinstance(metrics, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"metrics must be an object when present\")\n    rubrics = normalized.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if rubrics is not None and not isinstance(rubrics, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"rubrics must be an array when present\")\n    tags = normalized.get(\"tags\")\n    if tags is not None:\n        if not isinstance(tags, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"tags must be an array when present\")\n        normalized[\"tags\"] = [str(item).strip() for item in tags if str(item).strip()]\n    return normalized\n\n\ndef _markdown_entry(event: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Handle markdown entry logic for this module.\"\"\"\n    lines = [\n        f\"### {event['timestamp']} | step={event['step']} | scope={event['scope']}\",\n        f\"- summary: {event['summary']}\",\n        f\"- evidence: {event['evidence']}\",\n        f\"- next_action: {event['next_action']}\",\n    ]\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = event.get(key)\n        if isinstance(value, str) and value.strip():\n            lines.append(f\"- {key}: {value.strip()}\")\n\n    metrics = event.get(\"metrics\")\n    if isinstance(metrics, dict) and metrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- metrics: {json.dumps(metrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    rubrics = event.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if isinstance(rubrics, list) and rubrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- rubrics: {json.dumps(rubrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    tags = event.get(\"tags\")\n    if isinstance(tags, list) and tags:\n        lines.append(f\"- tags: {', '.join(str(item) for item in tags)}\")\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef _append_text(path: Path, text: str, *, header: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Safely initialize and append text to a regular file.\"\"\"\n    fd = _open_regular_for_append(path)\n    try:\n        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n        size = os.fstat(fd).st_size\n        if not size:\n            _write_all(fd, header.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n        elif os.pread(fd, 1, size - 1) != b\"\\n\":\n            _write_all(fd, b\"\\n\")\n        _write_all(fd, text.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n    finally:\n        try:\n            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n        finally:\n            os.close(fd)\n\n\ndef _append_jsonl(path: Path, payload: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Append one JSON object as a JSONL record.\"\"\"\n    line = (json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\").encode(\"utf-8\")\n    fd = _open_regular_for_append(path)\n    try:\n        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n        size = os.fstat(fd).st_size\n        if size and os.pread(fd, 1, size - 1) != b\"\\n\":\n            _write_all(fd, b\"\\n\")\n        _write_all(fd, line)\n    finally:\n        try:\n            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n        finally:\n            os.close(fd)\n\n\ndef _open_regular_for_append(path: Path) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Open an append target without following its parent or leaf.\"\"\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
