{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json,re,hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\ntext=Path('paper.tex').read_text()\nbib=set(re.findall(r'@\\\\w+\\\\s*\\\\{\\\\s*([\"'^,]+)'\"',Path('references.bib').read_text()))\ncited={key.strip() for block in re.findall(r'\\\\\\\\cite\\\\w*\\\\s*\\\\{([\"'^}]+)'\"\\\\}',text) for key in block.split(',')}\nprovenance=json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())\nrecords={item['citation_key']:item for item in provenance['references']}\nprint('Citation keys:',len(cited),'BibTeX:',len(bib),'Provenance:',len(records))\nprint('Missing BibTeX:',sorted(cited-bib),'Missing provenance:',sorted(cited-records.keys()))\nfor key in sorted(cited):\n    record=records[key]\n    artifact=record.get('consulted_artifact')\n    print(key,'|',record.get('consultation_level'),'| artifact exists:',bool(artifact and Path(artifact).exists()))\nstrategy=json.loads(Path('paper_strategy.json').read_text())\nprint('Question:',strategy['central_question'])\nprint('Writer notes:',json.dumps(strategy['notes_for_writer']))\nprint('Sections:',re.findall(r'\\\\\\\\section\\\\{([\"'^}]+)'\"\\\\}',text))\nfor name in ['paper.tex','references.bib','references_provenance.json']:\n    print('Protected SHA256:',name,hashlib.sha256(Path(name).read_bytes()).hexdigest())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json,re,hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\ntext=Path('paper.tex').read_text()\nbib=set(re.findall(r'@\\\\w+\\\\s*\\\\{\\\\s*([\"'^,]+)'\"',Path('references.bib').read_text()))\ncited={key.strip() for block in re.findall(r'\\\\\\\\cite\\\\w*\\\\s*\\\\{([\"'^}]+)'\"\\\\}',text) for key in block.split(',')}\nprovenance=json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())\nrecords={item['citation_key']:item for item in provenance['references']}\nprint('Citation keys:',len(cited),'BibTeX:',len(bib),'Provenance:',len(records))\nprint('Missing BibTeX:',sorted(cited-bib),'Missing provenance:',sorted(cited-records.keys()))\nfor key in sorted(cited):\n    record=records[key]\n    artifact=record.get('consulted_artifact')\n    print(key,'|',record.get('consultation_level'),'| artifact exists:',bool(artifact and Path(artifact).exists()))\nstrategy=json.loads(Path('paper_strategy.json').read_text())\nprint('Question:',strategy['central_question'])\nprint('Writer notes:',json.dumps(strategy['notes_for_writer']))\nprint('Sections:',re.findall(r'\\\\\\\\section\\\\{([\"'^}]+)'\"\\\\}',text))\nfor name in ['paper.tex','references.bib','references_provenance.json']:\n    print('Protected SHA256:',name,hashlib.sha256(Path(name).read_bytes()).hexdigest())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Citation keys: 25 BibTeX: 25 Provenance: 25\nMissing BibTeX: [] Missing provenance: []\nBradley1952 | bibliographic record only | artifact exists: True\nBroderick2020 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nChiang2024 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nCook1977 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nDavidson1970 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nDavison1997 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nEfron1979 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nField2007 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nFirth1993 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nFord1957 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nGiordano2019 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nHampel1974 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nHunter2004 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nKendall1938 | bibliographic record only | artifact exists: True\nKoh2017 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nMin2025 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nNBAdata | dataset documentation | artifact exists: True\nNegahban2012 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nOwen2007 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nPlackett1975 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nRubin1981 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nShah2017 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nThurstone1927 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nTurner2012 | abstract | artifact exists: True\nZermelo1929 | bibliographic record only | artifact exists: True\nQuestion: How do small, influence-ordered deletions affect regularized Bradley–Terry rankings, and how does their disruption compare with random and high-loss deletion across crowd preferences and historical sports outcomes?\nWriter notes: [\"Scope: this strategy writes neither paper.tex nor claims_grounding.json, drafts no final paper, renders no figures, runs no new experiment, and invokes no final-paper validation. Dotted JSON fields, internal selection terms and hashes in this memo are private-only source maps, not visible manuscript labels. Memory is qualitative planning context only.\", \"Venue/layout: use VENUE.md and the supplied ICLR 2026 style. The inspected paper.sty has textwidth=5.5 inches and textheight=9 inches, single-column: column width equals full text width. All three figures use this text block, not a two-column figure* layout. Keep margins and typography unchanged.\", \"Body budget, approximately 8.5 pages including figures/tables but excluding references: title/abstract 0.5; introduction 1.0; related work 0.6; method 1.6; data/metrics/uncertainty protocol 1.1; results 2.6; discussion/limitations 0.8; conclusion 0.3. These are planned page equivalents, not measured pagination. Venue requires 8\\u20139 body pages; an eight-page body must end at least 75% full. Spend space on scientific explanation, not padding or unsupported experiments.\", \"Thesis-first headings: Introduction; Related Work; Frozen-Prefix Ranking Audits; Data, Metrics, and Uncertainty; Dataset- and Budget-Dependent Disruption; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. Use three figures plus two compact tables: final aggregate metrics with seed-interval interpretation, and descriptive search configurations. Keep search context brief and distinct from final evidence.\", \"Protocol from inspected code: mean negative log-likelihood plus lambda=0.001 ridge, centered scores, ties as half wins, nominal deletion fractions 0.1%, 0.5%, 1%, floored row counts. For removed prefix S of size k among n rows, the screening displacement is H_clean inverse applied to (sum of removed row gradients + k*lambda*theta_clean), divided by n-k. Distinguish that approximation from converged retained-data fits; exact means residual-controlled numerical refitting, not symbolic exactness.\", \"Definitions: normalized inversion fraction divides discordant participant pairs by all participant pairs. Normalized original-leader rank drop divides its downward position change by participant count minus one. Per-budget curves are inversions, not leader drops. The selector uses leader-drop objectives, which need not optimize the reported inversion statistic. Larger disruption does not imply ranking inaccuracy or better models.\", \"Comparison scope: row fraction normalizes intervention size, not effective sample size, participant exposure, graph geometry, leverage or uncertainty. Two unmatched designs do not identify a causal design effect. NBA historical team codes/eras are heterogeneous. Fit-specific ranking sensitivity is not evidence about present-day platform rankings or participant ability across eras.\", \"Uncertainty: the aggregate high-loss-relative seed interval is [0.002381968563475412, 0.002381968563475412]; the random-relative interval is [0.007377907506332164, 0.008168732424939618]. Source each endpoint with its final.metric.paired_gain_*_ci_* ID. Explain seed-resampling construction in the main table caption. Repeated deterministic contrasts do not estimate data uncertainty.\", \"Conditional group resampling holds original masks fixed, refits weighted data, and does not rerun contender selection or either baseline order. Removed weighted mass is not fixed by nominal row fraction. There are 32 unique stored records per dataset, repeated across exported episodes; never pool these into 160 independent records. No full-procedure confidence or population-wide significance claim.\", \"No matched-support experiment, whole-group deletion frontier, expert/judge comparison, adaptive order refinement, ridge-sensitivity study, runtime ablation or global minimum-deletion certificate was measured. Provenance groups support split/resampling only; the selector receives anonymous rows. Do not turn implementation intent into empirical findings.\", \"Qualification: current authoritative final sources report completed and qualified. This does not establish generalization or universal superiority. If later authoritative evidence reports failed qualification, disclose and preserve it through writing, review, audit and revision; distinguish statistical/performance causes from validity/adaptivity causes only when identified by evaluator diagnostics. Missing causes stay unknown.\", \"Source map: final.evidence.episodes supports per-case data and conditional resampling; final.metric.* supports aggregate metrics; final.qualification.* alone grounds qualification. No downstream_study or study.* sources exist, so omit campaign selection advantages, derived search-score differences, attempt counts and original-starter quantitative comparison. Use result.top_program_* only for clearly labeled descriptive raw search scores. Unscored performance is missing, not a loss.\", \"Positioning: claim an auditable fitted-ranking protocol, measured two-setting budget contrasts and conditional uncertainty with limitations. Do not claim new Bradley\\u2013Terry estimation, novelty priority, universally effective attacks, or causal effects of evaluation design. The two exact-refit configurations share a search aggregate, not proven equivalence; no comparative CPU-cost claim is available.\", \"References: staged retrieval has irrelevant matches, duplicate Bradley\\u2013Terry records, and lacks several exact planned influence-function, finite-sample robustness, Arena, vote-rigging and NBA provenance identities. Later verify exact allowed identities and actually consult their content; use synchronized BibTeX/provenance keys only. Existing matches are not citation permission. No broad leaderboard searches, citation traversal, guessing of the prohibited work, or citations to unconsulted material. This strategy makes no network requests.\", \"Figure outputs: quantitative plots require reproducible source, vector PDF and 300-DPI PNG. LaTeX must reference PDF whenever it exists. Prefer editable draw.io plus PDF/PNG for the concept overview; if raster-only, require at least 2400 px width for these full-width figures, or 1200 px for any later justified column-scale raster. Regenerate rather than upscale. Follow concept-figure orchestration later; do not render during strategy generation.\", \"Readability: labels should render at 9\\u201310 pt or larger. Method colors stay consistent within the comparison; dataset colors in the uncertainty figure have an explicitly different labeled role. A zero reference is not another method. No thresholded success-rate plot is warranted. Simplify or regenerate dense figures rather than shrinking.\", \"Supplement: substantive material already exists. After references use a clear page, appendix mode, and Supplementary Information in the same paper source; include a separate LLM Usage subsection. Authoritative posthoc rankings arrive separately; route appendix-ranked analyses there without guessing rankings now or moving central evidence out of the main text. The five source-backed supplementary entries above describe scientific evidence; the separate mandatory LLM Usage subsection is a process disclosure, not an additional result-grounded entry. Disclose the roles documented in supplied agent-run logs and artifacts: research ideation, candidate-code generation, reference-query planning, and manuscript assistance. Distinguish these from the numerical evaluator. Do not invent provider/model identities, human oversight or paid-API experiments; this is process provenance, not a numerical result.\", \"Anonymity: omit names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, self-identifying links and internal URLs. Remove template final-copy/author scaffolding during drafting while preserving its required watermark. Include the separate LLM Usage disclosure; do not invent a mandatory checklist not supplied for this venue.\", \"Reproducibility: inspected sources include the candidate, evaluator, normalized resources/manifests and numpy==2.2.6, scipy==1.15.3 requirements. A complete raw-to-partition builder and all raw originals are not staged. Inventory actual available artifacts/commands and distinguish staged-resource reruns from raw-source reconstruction. Do not claim the broader reproduction package is already complete.\"]\nSections: ['Introduction', 'Related Work', 'Method', 'Experimental Setup', 'Results', 'Discussion and Limitations', 'Conclusion', 'Supplementary Information']\nProtected SHA256: paper.tex 1a19430860af50a65d4078357da1c1550b9068c65aecfdc11696db3a9889c43e\nProtected SHA256: references.bib efcd95126132898485591de400f98f0a19416cb0371c8017bf0e8343b0dab191\nProtected SHA256: references_provenance.json a1c08e1ba0031fd544d37f46e5f63e95ea95534630b5fbbe021ee9213d09eef1\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
